Call of Duty 2: Big Red One - PC port, prototype @PROJECT_VERSION@
=================================================================

Runs the original Xbox game natively on Linux. It needs your own copy of the
game; no game files are included.

This is a prototype: the single-player campaign is playable, missions 1 to 5
have been tested through. Multiplayer is not supported.


Setup
-----

Copy your game dump into the assets folder.

Then start cod_bro_launcher. It shows whether the game files are found, lets
you use another folder instead, sets the options below, and starts the game.
(cod_bro_loader starts the game directly with the saved settings.)


Requirements
------------

- Linux on a 64-bit (or 32-bit) x86 PC, glibc @COD_BRO_GLIBC_MIN@ or newer.
- 32-bit graphics and sound libraries, the same ones 32-bit games need (they come
  with Steam on most distributions): a Vulkan driver (Mesa or NVIDIA, 32-bit),
  the X11 or Wayland client libraries, and PulseAudio or PipeWire client libraries.
- A GPU with Vulkan 1.3 support.

The other libraries are in lib/ (see LICENSES/BUNDLED.txt).


Controls
--------

Gamepads use their Xbox layout. Keyboard and mouse:

  WASD           move                 mouse          look
  left mouse     fire                 right mouse    aim down sights
  Space          jump                 C / Ctrl       crouch, prone
  R              reload               F              use
  G              grenade              V / middle     melee
  left Shift     sprint               Q / E          lean
  wheel / 1      next weapon          Tab (hold)     objectives
  Escape         pause                F10            free the mouse

Menus: arrow keys, Return selects, Backspace goes back. Click the window to
capture the mouse; Alt+Tab or F10 frees it.


Options
-------

The launcher saves its settings in ~/.local/share/cod_bro/settings.ini, next to
the saves. Every setting is also a command-line option of cod_bro_loader, which
then wins over the file; ./cod_bro_loader --help lists them.


